`CLOSED_CERTIFIED_H11_SELECTED710_AFFINE_SOURCE_RHS_ON_EMBEDDINGS4_AND5`

G3DD carries the complete G3DC source operator into the source-independent 710-dimensional path kernel selected by G3CY and certified by G3DB.

## First reduction

Write

```text
X_B89 = A0^-1 B_B89,
X_C   = A0^-1 B_C,
Y_B89 = W X_B89,
Y_C   = W X_C,
Z_B89 = S^-1 Y_B89,
Z_C   = S^-1 Y_C.
```

The exact `W` support observes only 1,186 of the 4,426 base coordinates. G3DD evaluates that corridor for all 496 source columns and solves the resulting `988 x 496` system. Every one of the 490,048 `S Z = W X` residual balls contains zero.

The emitted `Z_B89` and `Z_C` archives each have shape `988 x 248` and retain at least 83 relative accuracy bits away from zero.

## Selected second reduction

Let `R` be the 710 exact rows selected by G3CY and put

```text
V     = Q[R,:],
H_B89 = V Z_B89,
H_C   = V Z_C.
```

G3CX proves that 248 columns of `Q` vanish exactly, so the contraction uses the complete 740-column active support. The two emitted `H` maps each have shape `710 x 248` and retain at least 77 relative accuracy bits away from zero.

## Selected source equation

For the evolving selected H20 state `c20(a)`, the first reduced equation is

```text
(S + a Q) z = a (Y_B89 + a Y_C)c20(a).
```

Its base `S` solution is

```text
z0 = a (Z_B89 + a Z_C)c20(a).
```

Applying the exact G3CY second Woodbury factorization gives the selected equation

```text
(T_Q + a R_Q)q = a^2 (H_B89 + a H_C)c20(a).
```

The matrix on the left is exactly the G3DB path kernel. Therefore both the kernel and its complete selected source operator are now emitted on embeddings 4 and 5 without benchmark rows or fitted values.

## Boundary

G3DD does not integrate `c20(a)`, solve the selected equation along G3BJ, recover the full 4,426-coordinate H11 state, or replay G3CT. Those are execution and validation steps downstream of source selection.

It does not select an Archimedean embedding physically, establish integral monodromy, or close either eta9 blocker.

